  "title": "An Exact Exterior Abel-Power Square Function for a Single Atom in ℝ³",
  "batch_label": "73",
  "kind": "resolution-paper",
  "original_status": "proved",
  "scope": "Under the Fourier convention f-hat(xi)=integral exp(-2 pi i x dot xi) f(x) dx, Delta=sum_j partial_j^2, H_t=exp(t Delta), A_s=s(s-Delta)^{-1}, and the cap-kappa radial partial-balayage domain Omega=B(0,R) with R^3=3m/(4 pi kappa), for every m>0, kappa>0, and integer N>=1, the exterior square function I_N=integral_{Omega^c} integral_0^infinity |s partial_s(A_s^N(m delta_0))(x)|^2 ds/s dx equals kappa*m*2*Gamma(N+3/2)^2/[3*pi*(N+1)*(N+2)*(2*N+1)*Gamma(N)^2]. Consequently I_N/(kappa*m) tends to 1/(3*pi) as N tends to infinity.",
